# FIXED-BLOCKS-AUDIT: the source tables of a program are as many, as wide and as large as it writes them
# (tests/unit_s7_tbl_many_part.lm2: twelve tables in all, one of 130 columns, one of five thousand cells,
# one cell of 300 bytes), and the conversion still finds `primitive.convert` by its name: a size_t given to an
# int place is converted.  The translation refused the part: "too many source tables", "a table has too many
# columns", "a table is too large", "a table cell is too long".  Entry 7.

fn: go () int
    int: a 1
    size_t: b 2U
    a: b
    return: a

int: k
k: go()
if: k = 2
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 1; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
